From: Hummingbird <hummingbird@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bump klauspost/compress v1.19.1->v1.20.2 for CVE-2026-116591

Upstream: https://github.com/klauspost/compress/commit/7f5d8528720c895a6106f201719f87eb030a565d

klauspost/compress before v1.20.2 panics in the zstd DecodeAll and
streaming decoder paths when a crafted two-block frame reaches
huff0.ReadTable with an FSE normalized count of 32768 stored in int16
as -32768.  The wrapped count lets buildDtable retain stale decode-table
state from the prior block; nextFast then derives an out-of-range state
and indexes past the table.  Untrusted zstd input can crash the process.
Fixed in v1.20.2 by rejecting normalized counts that do not fit in int16.

Grafana exposes this via its unified-storage Parquet reader and the
Badger v4 key-value store, both of which call zstd.DecodeAll or
zstd.NewReader on data that can originate from untrusted sources.

Updated vendor tarball (Source1) holds the v1.20.2 compress vendor tree
and the corrected vendor/modules.txt entry.  This patch updates only
go.mod and go.sum.

